<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan March farm import value up 26.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan March farm import value up 26.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's agricultural imports in March was US$279.1 million, a 26.4 percent rise from US$220.8 million in March 1996, the Finance Ministry said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Grain and oilseeds were Taiwan's top farm imports in March.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the rise in March import values to high world prices for grain and oilseeds during the period.</p>
<p>March import tonnages were not available, but traders estimated that 500,000 tonnes of corn and 260,000 tonnes of soybean would have arrived at Taiwan ports during March.</p>
<p>Major grain import figures (in million US$):</p>
<p>			   March 1997	 March 1996</p>
<p> Wheat			 29.5		 13.6</p>
<p> Corn			  87.3		 83.4</p>
<p> Soybeans		    94.0		 68.6</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
